„­bible_version£KJV¤book§chapter¨sections•…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙûNow it came to pass on the third day, that Esther put on her royal apparel, and stood in the inner court of the king's house, over against the king's house: and the king sat upon his royal throne in the royal house, over against the gate of the house.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙñAnd it was so, when the king saw Esther the queen standing in the court, that she obtained favour in his sight: and the king held out to Esther the golden sceptre that was in his hand. So Esther drew near, and touched the top of the sceptre.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‹Then said the king unto her, What wilt thou, queen Esther? and what is thy request? it shall be even given thee to the half of the kingdom.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‡And Esther answered, If it seem good unto the king, let the king and Haman come this day unto the banquet that I have prepared for him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ–Then the king said, Cause Haman to make haste, that he may do as Esther hath said. So the king and Haman came to the banquet that Esther had prepared.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¹And the king said unto Esther at the banquet of wine, What is thy petition? and it shall be granted thee: and what is thy request? even to the half of the kingdom it shall be performed.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ>Then answered Esther, and said, My petition and my request is;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙôif I have found favour in the sight of the king, and if it please the king to grant my petition, and to perform my request, let the king and Haman come to the banquet that I shall prepare for them, and I will do to morrow as the king hath said.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verse	ªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÂThen went Haman forth that day joyful and with a glad heart: but when Haman saw Mordecai in the king's gate, that he stood not up, nor moved for him, he was full of indignation against Mordecai.¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
