„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙĞAnd Haman told them of the glory of his riches, and the multitude of his children, and all the things wherein the king had promoted him, and how he had advanced him above the princes and servants of the king.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙºHaman said moreover, Yea, Esther the queen did let no man come in with the king unto the banquet that she had prepared but myself; and to morrow am I invited unto her also with the king.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ_Yet all this availeth me nothing, so long as I see Mordecai the Jew sitting at the king's gate.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚ*Then said Zeresh his wife and all his friends unto him, Let a gallows be made of fifty cubits high, and to morrow speak thou unto the king that Mordecai may be hanged thereon: then go thou in merrily with the king unto the banquet. And the thing pleased Haman; and he caused the gallows to be made.¦layout ªlast_verse